          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On May 28, 1977, starting at 3:00 AM, a student made three observations of a luminous phenomenon that intrigued her. A yellow ball moved slowly before disappearing. No noise was heard during the observation. Another witness arrived at the observation location the following day between 2:00 AM and 4:00 AM. Vertically above the observation point indicated by the first witness, this person observed the presence of the Moon. The student likely made an astronomical observation of the Moon.",
